 "conclusion": "All three synthetic panels are bit-identical with and without the gate, so it costs no event recall, precision or localisation there - but the synthetic scenes never bend the alignment, so the panels prove the absence of a regression and not the presence of a benefit. On the six recordings in-envelope clusters fall 5635 -> 3749 (-33 percent) and candidates stay at 11. The gate fires on 0-19 percent of frames per recording, almost entirely in the three recordings that show centre lock failures, and costs a median 20-25 m of certified horizon in the frames where it fires. One recording regresses: roundT_pressureGate_roundT rises 475 -> 536 clusters, consistent with a truncated chain leaving a noisier two-anchor tangent that can swing the envelope. Fewer in-envelope clusters is not a measured precision gain: without exhaustive negative episodes it cannot be shown that what was removed was infrastructure rather than real support."
